<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhu Fan Zhi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1225">1225</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zhu Fan Zhi ('Records of Foreign Peoples') is a Chinese work completed around 1225 by Zhao Rugua, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> superintendent of maritime trade at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quanzhou">Quanzhou</a>. Based on interviews with merchants and sailors, it describes the countries, peoples and goods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> and beyond, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> and Ma-i to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>. It is a key source for Asian maritime trade in the Song period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhu-fan-zhi.jpg" alt="Zhu Fan Zhi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zhao Ru Kuo (Chinese:趙汝适, 1170-1228) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%AB%B8%E8%95%83%E5%BF%97%EF%BC%88%E5%9B%9B%E5%BA%AB%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Zhu Fan Zhi</b> of about 1225 says officials boarded each arriving ship with a leather-bound register, took 20 per cent of the cargo as tax and confiscated the whole if anything was hidden.</blockquote><a href="/empire/champa">Champa · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Zhao Rugua's <b>Zhufan zhi</b> of 1225 describes a settlement of over a thousand families on a river, whose chief used a white umbrella.</blockquote><a href="/state/ma-i">Ma-i</a></li></ul></section>
